<div class="post">
<h2>June 18, 2006</h2>


<h1 id="a000110">So Long Brian,  Hello Bora Bora</h1>

<p><a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/theroadislife/170187944/" title="Photo Sharing"><img src="http://static.flickr.com/65/170187944_59f9d10edd_m.jpg" width="240" height="180" hspace="10" vspace="10" align="left" alt="Blithe Spirit Moored in Tahaa" /></a>TAHAA, FRENCH POLYNESIA - Things have changed dramatically since finding our luggage.   Brian has decided to fly back to Canada in order to pursue some potentially lucrative money-making options for the summer.  He's promised to rejoin the trip as soon as possible,  I on the other hand am determined to soldier onward despite the costs involved.   I'm drooling over the prospect of finding work in Australia or New Zealand in the next few months.</p>

<p>Two days ago, opportunity knocked for me.  I may have found my magic ticket the rest of the way across the Pacific aboard a very fast and very interesting ocean racing catamaran (pictured above).</p>

<p>In fact I've already left Tahiti and am anchored in a sheltered bay on a picture perfect island called <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tahaa">Tahaa</a> near <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bora_Bora">Bora Bora</a> after sailing overnight from Tahiti.   The rumor is that some weather may be hitting on Tuesday and my new skipper thought it best to get out of Tahiti and into a more sheltered anchorage.  Once the weather clears we'll probably sail on to Bora Bora then out of French Polynesia and onward toward <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tonga">Tonga</a> or <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiji">Fiji</a>.</p>

<p>The new boat, <em>Blithe Spirit</em>, is returning to Australia to complete a circumnavigation after performing very well  (4th) in a trans-Atlantic race from South Africa to Brazil and successfully warding off pirates in Venezuela.   The skipper seems to be a wealth of knowledge and experience.   We are 4 people including the Captain, myself and two other Australians; Cam is my age and Richard is 17 but has more sailing experience than you'd expect from someone so young.</p>

<p><em>*Internet is rumored to cost more than $24 USD in Bora Bora.  I'll try to get something up when we arrive though; however brief.</em><br />
</p>



